module tumta/main;

// Surface-Kio coverage of `_`-marked type-arg slots at call
// sites: the typer treats each `_` as an elided positional
// type-arg the same way as the fully-elided form. Exercises
// both inference paths in one call — `__left__`'s first
// binder is solved by value-arg unification, the second by the
// return type — the same dual-path setup the sibling Kio'
// golden `typecheck_return_type_inference` uses for its
// elided-form variant.
//
// `_` in call-arg position is surface sugar only (per
// `specs/prime.md` § 41, Kio' has no inference), so this
// case is non-Kio' (no IS_KIO_PRIME marker).
import __intrinsics__;

import tumta(String);

// `__left__ : [A][B](x: A) -> (a | B)`. Two positional
// `_` slots in front of `x` stand in for the two type-args; the
// typer solves `[A] = .` from `x`'s type and `[B] = String`
// from the return type.
fn mk_left_str_marked(x: .) -> . | String { __left__(_, _, x) }
